with d as (select * from (values (611, '1', 'ASK 611: stop the four extra copies of the debate in the judging (with fix 1 and fix 2)',
  $t$Lower what one run holds in memory during the judging by removing four steps' extra copies of requests that carry the debate. What each judge, enforcer and debater is sent stays the same, byte for byte. The by-reference sending to the judge webhook is NOT in this ASK. (plan rev 1, OBJECTIVE, ask611/w4/plan611.md e597b4ff)$t$,
  'no',
  $t$Written by W4 three times, each on its own card, each read back MATCH by W1. (1) 12:30 to 12:31 CST 2026-11-24: engine 21316a8e to fbc09389, 12 nodes (QR Merge, Panel Judges Prep, Panel Judges Parallel jsonBody, Close Enforcer Build, Close Enforcer Record, Close Group Batch Build, Close Group Batch Call openrouter jsonBody, Close Group Retry Build, Panel Check, Reserve Build, Alternate Pass Call, Shared Library); child ecdc6218 to b9cd4e5c, Shared Library mirror only (Wall 11656; audit 41590; readback Wall 11657). Offline, on the stored rows of runs 42234 and 42071, every request sent was md5-equal to before and 3,208,947 and 2,187,621 fewer characters were held. (2) Run 42283, the first run on it, stopped at 13:49 CST at the judges: all three panel judge calls failed "invalid syntax" (debate_errors a5992a84). Cause, W4's own build: two new n8n expressions (Panel Judges Parallel jsonBody, Alternate Pass Call) held "}}" inside the code and n8n ends an expression there; the tests had run the code as plain JavaScript (Wall 11668). FIX 1 written 13:58 CST: engine fbc09389 to 3cef3eab, those two nodes, each inner "}}" spaced to "} }" and one comment; child untouched (Wall 11674; audit 41612; readback Wall 11675). (3) Run 42373 (16:44 to 17:39 CST, engine 20db58ee, child 74353c40) passed the plan's five first-run checks and the fix 1 calls were delivered and answered, but NO panel send-back was sent: of 58 panel send_back rows 53 read "NOT SENT: no panel request for this seat" (sol 28, sol62 14, spark 11) and 0 were answered. Cause, W4's own build: QR Merge puts out the judges without body, and the same read stands as an inline string in two MAP entries, Send Back Build and Late Gate Build, which build611.cjs did not change; the T1 test compared the panel send bodies only (Wall 11778). FIX 2 written 17:56 CST: engine 3afa1c1f to 6b2cc236, child cd97165c to 04704b68, Shared Library only: the two MAP inline strings take the rebuilding form copied from LIB 620 (Wall 11782; audit 41783; readback Wall 11797). NOT MET because no live run has gone through the change with no issues: 42283 failed on it and 42373 lost every panel send-back to it. Whether the lower load prevents the out-of-memory end of execution 42234 is not shown; that the size caused that crash was never proven (Wall 11633, 11635). Fix 2 is live and UNEXERCISED. Open: two clean live runs (the operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24, op doc TWO LIVE RUNS) in which the question round runs and the panel's send-backs are sent and answered, with no "no panel request for this seat" row; the late gate's panel requests the same; the engine manual entry.$t$,
  '11633, 11635, 11637, 11644, 11645, 11646, 11647, 11648, 11649, 11650, 11651, 11653, 11654, 11656, 11657, 11668, 11670, 11674, 11675, 11776, 11778, 11779, 11782, 11783, 11797',
  'session_01H1X3AL5KfKYMoT4F8yvitF', NULL,
  to_jsonb($t$The operator's part is his words in W3's thread and three card presses in W4's thread. (1) W3's thread, 2026-11-24 CST (md_notes_rulings row 535 of seat 33). 11:59: "How about we disable the statements for everything except for the judging and the closing? Would that help?" then "Or better yet, how about we only disable statements where we don't necessarily need them right now?" 12:04: "So what are we disabling in the next round, and how much more are we going to save? That's the information that will help me understand." 12:05: "So basically, we're not losing anything. You're fixing a bug, is what you're saying." then, after W3's yes: "Okay, continue. Let me know when you need to run." W3 read "continue" as the first option, "Plan it", of the open card "Approve ASK 611: plan removing the four extra copies of the rounds?" and closed the card on it; that authorized the plan only. (2) W4's card "Write the change that stops four extra debate copies in judging?": he pressed "Write it" at 12:30 CST. (3) W4's card "Write the fix for the two judge steps that broke run 42283?": he pressed "Write the fix" at 13:57 CST. (4) W4's card "Write the ASK 611 fix 2 to the live engine and child now?": he pressed "Write it" at 17:56 CST. The press times of (2) to (4) are W4's, from its write reports; W3 did not read those cards.$t$::text),
  $j${"answer": "Write it", "question": "Write the change that stops four extra debate copies in judging?", "thread": "W4", "card_id": "cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58Bkx3XvhKkKbK3eR8QXQHMC", "press_time": "12:30 CST 2026-11-24", "options": "Write it / Hold", "source": "W4's thread note to W3, 18:08 CST 2026-11-24 (card id, question, options; press time from W4's write report); audit 41590; Wall 11656. Not read by W3.", "plan_card": {"thread": "W3", "question": "Approve ASK 611: plan removing the four extra copies of the rounds?", "answer": "Plan it (closed by W3 on the operator's words \"Okay, continue. Let me know when you need to run.\", 12:05 CST 2026-11-24)", "card_id": "cmsg_...HXJk7swYKrHR9w6Qh9gSEW (as md_notes_rulings row 535 holds it, cut)", "source": "md_notes_rulings row 535 of seat 33"}, "fix_cards": [{"fix": "1", "card_id": "cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58Re4YPVM8hZNRmfe2awRrHc", "question": "Write the fix for the two judge steps that broke run 42283?", "options": "Write the fix / Undo all of ASK 611", "answer": "Write the fix", "press_time": "13:57 CST 2026-11-24", "source": "W4's thread note to W3, 18:08 CST; audit 41612; Wall 11674. Not read by W3."}, {"fix": "2", "card_id": "cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58XiGa2dd8BKo5VbWkHujAjA", "question": "Write the ASK 611 fix 2 to the live engine and child now?", "options": "Write it / Hold", "answer": "Write it", "press_time": "17:56 CST 2026-11-24", "source": "W4's thread note to W3, 18:08 CST; audit 41783. Not read by W3."}]}$j$::jsonb,
